The analysis reveals significant changes between versions 1.14.1 and 1.13.1 of `org.jsoup:jsoup`, particularly around the `Safelist` and `Whitelist` classes. The trace divergence indicates that the `Safelist` class in version 1.14.1 has been replaced or significantly altered in version 1.13.1, where it is referred to as `Whitelist`. This is a key point of failure in the test execution.

### Diagnosis
The primary issue stems from the renaming or restructuring of the `Safelist` class (in 1.14.1) to `Whitelist` (in 1.13.1). This change affects method calls and initializations involving `Safelist`, leading to test failures in both baseline and target executions.

